module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.CompletedConnection
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.QuotEquivMapPowModule

/-!
# Associativity of the completed tensor product along a base change

The row comparison in the proof of [Stacks, Proposition 60.21.3, Tag 07LG] needs, in each
cosimplicial degree `b`, an identification

`M(b) ⊗̂_{D(b)} Ω^a_{D(b)} ≅ M ⊗̂_D Ω^a_{D(b)}`,

and the source gets it from two facts: that `M(b)` is the base change `M ⊗̂_D D(b)`, and that the
completed tensor product is associative, so that `(M ⊗̂_D D(b)) ⊗̂_{D(b)} Ω = M ⊗̂_D Ω`.  **This
module proves the second fact.**  The first is the crystal property and is not proved here; see
the module documentation of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/Computes07LGFromDoubleComplex.lean` and of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/Cosimplicial/CosimplicialStructurePair.lean`, where
the only term of `Crystalline.CosimplicialCompletedPair` in the library is the one for the
coefficient sheaf `𝒪_{X/S}`.

## What is proved

For a ring map `D → D'`, a `D'`-module `Ω` and a `D`-module `M`,

`Crystalline.CompletedTensor p D' Ω (D' ⊗_D M) ≃+ Crystalline.CompletedTensor p D Ω M`,

the base change being the *uncompleted* one `D' ⊗_D M`.  Three things happen, and the third is
the one that is not formal:

* the uncompleted cancellation `(D' ⊗_D M) ⊗_{D'} Ω ≅ Ω ⊗_D M`, which is
  `TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange` after a commutation, `D'`-linearly;
* the commutation `Ω ⊗_D M ≅ M ⊗_D Ω`, `D`-linearly;
* the change of the ring the completion is taken over.  `Crystalline.CompletedTensor p D' Ω -`
  completes along `(p) ⊆ D'` and `Crystalline.CompletedTensor p D Ω -` along `(p) ⊆ D`, and
  these are ideals of two different rings.  They cut out the *same* filtration of any module
  carrying compatible actions of both, both being generated by the image of the integer `p`, and
  that is `adicCompletionLinearEquivMapModule` of
  `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/AdicCompletion/QuotEquivMapPowModule.lean`.

Because the first two steps are linear over the two different rings, the composite is stated as
an additive equivalence.  What pins it down is
`Crystalline.completedTensorCancelBaseChange_of_tmul`: it carries the class of
`(d' ⊗ m) ⊗ ω` to the class of `m ⊗ (d' • ω)`, which is the map the source writes down.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.tensorCancelBaseChange` — the uncompleted cancellation
  `(D' ⊗_D M) ⊗_{D'} Ω ≅ Ω ⊗_D M`.
* `Crystalline.completedTensorCancelBaseChange` — **the identification.**

## Main results

* `Crystalline.completedTensorCancelBaseChange_of_tmul` — its value on the canonical image of
  `(d' ⊗ m) ⊗ ω`.

No tag attribute is placed: associativity of the completed tensor product is not a tag of the
chapter, it is a step inside the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07LG].

## References

* [Stacks Project, Proposition 60.21.3, Tag 07LG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07LG)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 60.17.5, Tag 07L2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07L2)
-/

@[expose] public section

open DividedPowers
open scoped TensorProduct

universe uD uD' uO uM

namespace Crystalline

variable (p : ℕ) (D : Type uD) [CommRing D] (D' : Type uD') [CommRing D'] [Algebra D D']
  (Omega : Type uO) [AddCommGroup Omega] [Module D Omega] [Module D' Omega]
  [IsScalarTower D D' Omega] (M : Type uM) [AddCommGroup M] [Module D M]

/-- The ideal `(p) ⊆ D'` is the image of the ideal `(p) ⊆ D`: both are generated by the image of
the integer `p`.  This is what lets the two completions of one module be compared. -/
public theorem pAdicIdeal_eq_map_algebraMap :
    pAdicIdeal (A := D') p = (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p).map (algebraMap D D') := by
  rw [pAdicIdeal, pAdicIdeal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_natCast]

/-- **The uncompleted cancellation `(D' ⊗_D M) ⊗_{D'} Ω ≅ Ω ⊗_D M`**, `D'`-linearly: the
commutation of the two factors followed by
`TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange`. -/
public noncomputable def tensorCancelBaseChange :
    (D' ⊗[D] M) ⊗[D'] Omega ≃ₗ[D'] Omega ⊗[D] M :=
  (TensorProduct.comm D' (D' ⊗[D] M) Omega).trans
    (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange D D' D' Omega M)

/-- `tensorCancelBaseChange` sends `(d ⊗ m) ⊗ ω` to `(d • ω) ⊗ m`. -/
@[simp] public theorem tensorCancelBaseChange_tmul_tmul (d : D') (m : M) (omega : Omega) :
    tensorCancelBaseChange D D' Omega M ((d ⊗ₜ m) ⊗ₜ omega) = (d • omega) ⊗ₜ m := rfl

/-- **Associativity of the completed tensor product along a base change:**
`(D' ⊗_D M) ⊗̂_{D'} Ω ≅ M ⊗̂_D Ω`.

The two completions are taken along the ideals `(p)` of the two different rings `D'` and `D`;
they cut out the same filtration of `Ω ⊗_D M`, which is
`adicCompletionLinearEquivMapModule`. -/
public noncomputable def completedTensorCancelBaseChange :
    CompletedTensor p D' Omega (D' ⊗[D] M) ≃+ CompletedTensor p D Omega M :=
  ((AdicCompletion.congr (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p)
        (tensorCancelBaseChange D D' Omega M)).toAddEquiv.trans
      (adicCompletionLinearEquivMapModule (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p) D' (Omega ⊗[D] M)
        (pAdicIdeal_eq_map_algebraMap p D D')).symm.toAddEquiv).trans
    (AdicCompletion.congr (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p)
      (TensorProduct.comm D Omega M)).toAddEquiv

/-- **The identification carries the class of `(d' ⊗ m) ⊗ ω` to the class of `m ⊗ (d' • ω)`**,
which is the map of the source.  The canonical image of the uncompleted tensor product is
`p`-adically dense, so this pins the identification down. -/
public theorem completedTensorCancelBaseChange_of_tmul (d : D') (m : M) (omega : Omega) :
    completedTensorCancelBaseChange p D D' Omega M
        (toCompletedTensor p D' Omega (D' ⊗[D] M) ((d ⊗ₜ m) ⊗ₜ omega)) =
      toCompletedTensor p D Omega M (m ⊗ₜ (d • omega)) := by
  have h2 : (adicCompletionLinearEquivMapModule (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p) D' (Omega ⊗[D] M)
        (pAdicIdeal_eq_map_algebraMap p D D')).symm
        (AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (Omega ⊗[D] M) ((d • omega) ⊗ₜ m)) =
      AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p) (Omega ⊗[D] M) ((d • omega) ⊗ₜ m) :=
    (LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq _).2
      (adicCompletionLinearEquivMapModule_of (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p) D' (Omega ⊗[D] M)
        (pAdicIdeal_eq_map_algebraMap p D D') ((d • omega) ⊗ₜ m)).symm
  change AdicCompletion.congr (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p) (TensorProduct.comm D Omega M)
      ((adicCompletionLinearEquivMapModule (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p) D' (Omega ⊗[D] M)
          (pAdicIdeal_eq_map_algebraMap p D D')).symm
        (AdicCompletion.congr (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (tensorCancelBaseChange D D' Omega M)
          (AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) ((D' ⊗[D] M) ⊗[D'] Omega)
            ((d ⊗ₜ m) ⊗ₜ omega)))) = _
  rw [show AdicCompletion.congr (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p)
        (tensorCancelBaseChange D D' Omega M)
        (AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) ((D' ⊗[D] M) ⊗[D'] Omega)
          ((d ⊗ₜ m) ⊗ₜ omega)) =
      AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (Omega ⊗[D] M) ((d • omega) ⊗ₜ m) from rfl,
    h2]
  rfl

end Crystalline

end
